#: includes/class-abilities.php:46
#: includes/class-admin.php:54
msgid "Asset Scanner"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:47
msgid "Scan the front end for scripts, styles, cookies and domains, and test turning scripts and styles off, deferring or delaying them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:86
msgid "Test rules: rule key => action. Keys are \"js:\" or \"css:\" followed by host and path without query string (e.g. \"js:example.com/wp-includes/js/jquery/jquery.min.js\"), or \"js#\"/\"css#\" followed by the element id of inline code (e.g. \"js#jquery-core-js-after\"). Get keys from get-page-assets. Actions: \"off\", \"defer\" or \"delay\" for script files; \"off\" or \"delay\" for inline scripts; \"off\" or \"defer\" for stylesheet files; \"off\" for inline styles. An empty string removes a rule (merge mode)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:100
msgid "A front-end page on this site: a full URL or a path such as \"/about/\". Defaults to the home page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:104
msgid "Get scan summary"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:105
msgid "Returns the latest scan: when it ran, how many pages, scripts, styles, cookies and domains it found, which page URLs were scanned, and how many test rules the current user has."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:111
msgid "Run scan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:112
msgid "Scans up to 10 front-end pages and stores every script, stylesheet, cookie and external domain found, with the plugin behind each. Without input it scans the pages chosen on the Pages tab, or the home page plus recent pages and posts. Takes a few seconds per page. Read the results with get-results."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:116
msgid "Page URLs to scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:117
msgid "IDs of published posts or pages to scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:126
msgid "Get scan results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:127
msgid "Lists results of the latest scan for one type: \"js\" (scripts), \"css\" (stylesheets), \"cookies\" (with category and the plugin or service that sets each one) or \"domains\" (external domains). Supports search, a first/third-party filter and paging."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:144
msgid "Get page assets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:145
msgid "Renders one page and lists every script and stylesheet on it in page order, with the rule key to use in test rules, the plugin or theme behind it, whether it is third-party, whether it blocks rendering, and the action the current test rules give it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:156
msgid "Get test rules"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:157
msgid "Returns the current user's saved test rules (the ones applied when they open a page with ?nahnuas_test=1)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:163
msgid "Set test rules"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:164
msgid "Saves the current user's test rules. They only affect pages that user opens with ?nahnuas_test=1 while logged in, never visitors. Mode \"merge\" (default) adds or changes the given rules (\"\" removes one); \"replace\" replaces all rules (an empty object clears them)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:178
msgid "Run test"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:179
msgid "Tests a page with scripts or styles turned off, deferred or delayed, without changing the live site. The server renders the page with the rules and returns what changed, render-blocking files before and after, and dependency warnings (scripts that will break because a file they need was held back). It also returns browser_url, a one-time link valid for 30 minutes: open it in a real browser, wait until the page shows \"Nahnu test report sent\", then call get-test-report with the token to get the JavaScript errors from the browser. Uses the saved test rules unless \"rules\" is given."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:193
msgid "Get test report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:194
msgid "Returns a test run started by run-test: the server analysis and, once its browser_url has been opened in a browser, the JavaScript errors, whether delayed scripts ran, and the page load time."
msgstr ""

