#: includes/class-admin.php:532
msgid "Using with Cache &amp; Performance Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:541
msgid "Preview any page with scripts or stylesheets turned off, deferred or delayed before you change your cache plugin. Add ?nahnuas_test=1 to a page address while logged in as an administrator. A panel lists every file on the page with the plugin behind it and shows any JavaScript errors your changes cause. Only you see the test; visitors always get the normal page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:550
msgid "JS Defer &amp; Delay"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:551
msgid "The JS tab lists every script loaded on your pages with its file path, version, defer/async status, first- or third-party origin, and the plugin that owns it. Use it to decide which scripts are safe to defer or delay in WP Rocket, LiteSpeed Cache, NitroPack, or Hummingbird. First-party plugin scripts such as the WooCommerce cart usually need to load immediately; third-party trackers such as Google Analytics or Hotjar are good candidates for delay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:560
msgid "CSS Exclusions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:561
msgid "The CSS tab identifies every stylesheet and its owning plugin. When combining or minifying CSS causes layout breaks, copy the file path directly into your cache plugin's exclusion list — WP Rocket, LiteSpeed Cache, and W3 Total Cache all support path-based exclusions. Render-blocking stylesheets from page builders like Elementor or Divi typically need to stay excluded from aggressive minification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:570
msgid "Cache Bypass for Dynamic Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:571
msgid "The Cookies tab lists every cookie your site sets. Cache plugins use cookies to decide whether to serve a cached page or bypass the cache — e.g. WooCommerce cart cookies, WPML language cookies, and login cookies must all bypass the cache. This tab gives you the exact cookie names to enter into your cache plugin's bypass rules, replacing guesswork with a real scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:581
msgid "Cookie Consent Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:582
msgid "Before configuring Complianz, CookieYes, or Real Cookie Banner, run a scan to get a complete, categorized cookie inventory. The plugin identifies 600+ known cookies from 400+ plugins and services — each tagged as Necessary, Preferences, Analytics, or Marketing — so you can populate your consent management platform with accurate data rather than relying on a generic auto-scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:591
msgid "Export &amp; Document"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:592
msgid "Every tab has a CSV export. Use this to document your site's asset inventory, share a JS/CSS list with a developer optimizing your Core Web Vitals, or keep a record of which third-party scripts were present on a given date. Particularly useful for agencies managing multiple client sites."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:600
msgid "Open Source Libraries & Credits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:612
msgid "600+ cookie patterns covering 400+ WordPress plugins and services, built and maintained as part of this plugin. Covers WooCommerce, membership plugins, LMS platforms, builders, security plugins, analytics services, ad networks, and more. No external API needed: the data is updated with plugin releases."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-admin.php:624
msgid "Built on WordPress core APIs: the WP HTTP API, dbDelta, the Options API, and admin-ajax. Follows WordPress coding standards and the plugin review guidelines."
msgstr ""

